3c/code\u003e format using the schedule’s time zone, that scheduled callbacks may start being placed.\u003c/p\u003e\n","required":false,"allow_nil":true,"allow_blank":true,"validator":"Must be a decimal number.","expected_type":"numeric","metadata":null,"show":true,"validations":[],"deprecated":false},{"name":"scheduled_callback_hours_close","full_name":"scheduled_callback_hours_close","description":"\n\u003cp\u003eThe time of day, in \u003ccode\u003eHHMM\u003c/code\u003e format using the schedule’s time zone, that scheduled callbacks stop being placed.\u003c/p\u003e\n","required":false,"allow_nil":true,"allow_blank":true,"validator":"Must be a decimal number.","expected_type":"numeric","metadata":null,"show":true,"validations":[],"deprecated":false},{"name":"enable_public_show","full_name":"enable_public_show","description":"\n\u003cp\u003ePublish this schedule’s posting instructions page. Turning this on requires the company to have completed identity verification.\u003c/p\u003e\n","required":false,"allow_nil":true,"allow_blank":true,"validator":"Must be a boolean value: 1, true, yes, on, 0, false, no, off","expected_type":"boolean","metadata":null,"show":true,"validations":[],"deprecated":false},{"name":"enable_public_index","full_name":"enable_public_index","description":"\n\u003cp\u003eList this schedule’s posting instructions page on the company’s public index.\u003c/p\u003e\n","required":false,"allow_nil":true,"allow_blank":true,"validator":"Must be a boolean value: 1, true, yes, on, 0, false, no, off","expected_type":"boolean","metadata":null,"show":true,"validations":[],"deprecated":false},{"name":"public_name","full_name":"public_name","description":"\n\u003cp\u003eThe title shown on this schedule’s public posting instructions page.\u003c/p\u003e\n","required":false,"allow_nil":true,"allow_blank":true,"validator":"Must be a String","expected_type":"string","metadata":null,"show":true,"validations":[],"deprecated":false},{"name":"public_description","full_name":"public_description","description":"\n\u003cp\u003eThe rich-text description shown on this schedule’s public posting instructions page.\u003c/p\u003e\n","required":false,"allow_nil":true,"allow_blank":true,"validator":"Must be a String","expected_type":"string","metadata":null,"show":true,"validations":[],"deprecated":false}],"returns":[],"examples":[],"metadata":null,"see":[],"headers":[],"show":true},{"doc_url":"/api/docs/1.0/schedules/make_call","name":"make_call","apis":[{"api_url":"/api/v1/schedules/make_call","http_method":"POST","short_description":"Call a lead immediately","deprecated":null}],"formats":null,"full_description":"\n\u003cp\u003ePlaces an outbound call immediately. This is the endpoint to use for a “promote” / “call now” action.\u003cbr\u003e \u003cbr\u003e \u003cstrong\u003eIdentifying who to call (choose one):\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e • \u003cstrong\u003elead_id\u003c/strong\u003e — dials that exact existing Lead. Its number is used as \u003ccode\u003eto\u003c/code\u003e and its schedule is used to dial. Nothing new is created, so a promote never produces a duplicate lead. This is the recommended option.\u003cbr\u003e • \u003cstrong\u003elead_token\u003c/strong\u003e (a Schedule’s “Leads API Key”) or \u003cstrong\u003eschedule_id\u003c/strong\u003e — identifies the Schedule to dial from. You must also pass \u003ccode\u003eto\u003c/code\u003e (the number to dial).\u003cbr\u003e \u003cbr\u003e \u003cstrong\u003eSchedule / lead distribution routing:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e The resolved schedule takes the same code path as \u003ccode\u003ePOST /api/v1/leads\u003c/code\u003e. If it is a lead-distribution (“router”) schedule, the matching distribution is resolved from the submitted \u003ccode\u003edata\u003c/code\u003e (eg \u003ccode\u003etraffic_source_id\u003c/code\u003e) and the call is routed to that distribution’s downstream target schedule. If no distribution matches, the request is rejected.\u003cbr\u003e \u003cbr\u003e \u003cstrong\u003eWhich lead gets dialed (when using lead_token/schedule_id + to):\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e • If a live lead is already enrolled in the resolved schedule for that number, it is reused and dialed — no duplicate is created (the “promote” case).\u003cbr\u003e • Otherwise a one-off, offer-owned lead is created and dialed. This places a single call without enrolling the contact into the schedule’s dialing cadence.\u003cbr\u003e \u003cbr\u003e \u003cstrong\u003eGuards enforced before dialing:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e • The schedule must be active.\u003cbr\u003e • Account CPS (calls per second) limit.\u003cbr\u003e • DNC / contact suppression rules.\u003cbr\u003e • The same number cannot be dialed more than once every 30 seconds.\u003cbr\u003e • The destination number must be valid.\u003cbr\u003e \u003cbr\u003e Returns a serialized Call record on success. Raises errors for an unknown lead_id, an unresolvable or inactive schedule, no matching lead distribution, invalid numbers, suppressed contacts, exceeded CPS, recently-dialed numbers, or duplicate concurrent leads.\u003c/p\u003e\n","errors":[],"params":[{"name":"lead_id","full_name":"lead_id","description":"\n\u003cp\u003eThe TrackDrive ID (UUID) of an existing Lead to dial. When provided, the call uses this exact lead — its number is dialed and its schedule is used — so \u003ccode\u003eto\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003elead_token\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003eschedule_id\u003c/code\u003e are not required and are ignored. This is the preferred way to promote a lead you already created, because it never creates a duplicate.\u003c/p\u003e\n","required":false,"allow_nil":false,"allow_blank":false,"validator":"Must be a String","expected_type":"string","metadata":null,"show":true,"validations":[],"deprecated":false},{"name":"schedule_id","full_name":"schedule_id","description":"\n\u003cp\u003eThe ID of the Schedule to dial from. Must belong to the current company and be active. Use this (or \u003ccode\u003elead_token\u003c/code\u003e) together with \u003ccode\u003eto\u003c/code\u003e when you are not passing a \u003ccode\u003elead_id\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","required":false,"allow_nil":false,"allow_blank":false,"validator":"Must be a valid foreign key reference to an {Schedule}[/api/docs/1.0/schedules/index.html]. Refer to: {/api/docs/1.0/schedules}[/api/docs/1.0/schedules/index.html]","expected_type":"string","metadata":null,"show":true,"validations":[],"deprecated":false},{"name":"lead_token","full_name":"lead_token","description":"\n\u003cp\u003eThe token for the Schedule where you want lead to originate. Get it from: \u003ca href=\"https://trackdrive.com/schedules\"\u003etrackdrive.com/schedules\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n","required":false,"allow_nil":false,"allow_blank":false,"validator":"Must be a String","expected_type":"string","metadata":null,"show":true,"validations":[],"deprecated":false},{"name":"to","full_name":"to","description":"\n\u003cp\u003eDestination phone number to dial. Must be a valid number and not suppressed. Required unless a \u003ccode\u003elead_id\u003c/code\u003e is provided (in which case the lead’s number is used).\u003c/p\u003e\n","required":false,"allow_nil":false,"allow_blank":false,"validator":"Must be a String","expected_type":"string","metadata":null,"show":true,"validations":[],"deprecated":false},{"name":"data","full_name":"data","description":"\n\u003cp\u003eOptional hash of additional lead attributes (eg \u003ccode\u003etraffic_source_id\u003c/code\u003e). Used to route the lead through a lead-distribution schedule and stored on any lead that is created.\u003c/p\u003e\n","required":false,"allow_nil":false,"allow_blank":false,"validator":"Must be a Hash","expected_type":"hash","metadata":null,"show":true,"validations":[],"deprecated":false}],"returns":[],"examples":[],"metadata":null,"see":[],"headers":[],"show":true},{"doc_url":"/api/docs/1.0/schedules/show","name":"show","apis":[{"api_url":